# Git branch default

- **`dev` is the integration baseline**; **`main` is protected**. Never edit or commit feature work directly on `main` or `dev`.
- **Always work on a feature branch.** If the checked-out branch is already something other than `main` or `dev`, **stay on it** — even when the task is unrelated.
- **Multi-agent / shared workspace:** When several agents (or parallel chats) are working on different things in the same checkout, they must **share that already-open feature branch**. Do not create a second branch just because the work is a different topic.
- Only create a new feature branch from `dev` when the current branch is `main` or `dev` (or the user explicitly asks for a new branch).
- Name new branches clearly for the work (e.g. `fix/…`, `feat/…`). Prefer the repo’s existing naming style.
- Only switch, rename, or delete branches when the user asks, or when creating a branch because you are on `main`/`dev` as above.
- Commit / push / PR only when the user asks.
